        "Application server demand = 540/1,800 = 0.3s/transaction; database server demand = 720/900 = 0.8s/transaction; the database server is the bottleneck — on this reasoning, dividing the application server's busy time by the database server's call count is treated as a valid way to compare the two devices' demands against each other.",
